.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="FreundlichIsotherm models the empirical power law q=K_fP^{1/n}, useful for a heterogeneous surface where Langmuir&#x27;s single-site-energy assumption breaks down. Unlike Langmuir, it has no saturation limit, so extrapolating it far beyond the fitted pressure range is unphysical. fit_freundlich recovers (Kf, n) via the standard log q vs. log P linearization.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/surface/freundlich/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_freundlich_isotherm_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/surface/freundlich/plot_01_freundlich_isotherm`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">The Freundlich adsorption isotherm</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/surface/freundlich/plot_01_freundlich_isotherm`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="LangmuirIsotherm models monolayer adsorption on a fixed pool of identical surface sites. Its fractional coverage \theta=KP/(1+KP) reaches exactly one-half at the half-saturation pressure P=1/K, and fit_langmuir recovers (K, qmax) from noisy loading-vs-pressure data via the standard 1/q-vs-1/P linearization.">

